  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Vance stops short of endorsing Trump’s claim that Iran was close to nuclear weapon",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/21/vance-trump-iran-nuclear-weapon",
      "description": "<p>US vice-president says it’s not his place to second-guess the president, but refrains from endorsing Trump’s claim </p><p>At a White House news conference on Friday, JD Vance stopped short of endorsing Donald Trump’s claim that Iran was so close to obtaining a nuclear weapon in February that it was essential for the US to go to war with the Islamic republic.</p><p>In the White House briefing room, Trump was asked about <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/18/us/politics/vance-trump-iran-2028-election-rubio.html\">reporting this week</a> that he was unhappy with the US vice-president’s statement blaming Republican losses in the midterm elections on the Iran war.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/21/vance-trump-iran-nuclear-weapon\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-21T17:24:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump says he wants ‘permanent’ deal to stop Iran getting nuclear weapons",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/11/21/21-11-clip-trump-iran-permanent-nuclear-deal?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "US President Donald Trump says he wants a permanent agreement to prevent Iran from developing nuclear weapons.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-11-21T18:05:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump gives Vance, Rubio public audition as 2028 succession race heats up",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-gives-vance-rubio-public-audition-as-2028-succession-race-heats-up-126112100074_1.html",
      "description": "Marco Rubio fidgeted and sighed.\nJD Vance smiled and furrowed his brow.\nFor 90 minutes, the secretary of state and the vice president, both potential 2028 presidential contenders, stood nearly shoulder to shoulder in matching outfits, an arm's length from President Donald Trump as he spoke to reporters crowded into the White House press briefing room.\nIt was the latest episode in the public audition on Friday that the president and former reality television star has appeared to delight in arranging for his potential successors as he nears his last two years in office.\nIn the same room months earlier, Rubio and Vance each took a turn defending the president and selling his agenda while filling in as White House press secretary. The president has also been known to quiz his public and private audiences on their opinions of the two men.\nVance and Rubio maintain that they're good friends and have both demurred about whether they'll seek the White House in the next presidential race. R",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-21T04:57:55"
    }
  ]
